@using Cinnamon.Web.Components
@page "/overview"

<div class="container">
    <div class="section-1 row">
            <div class="col-lg-4 pt-5">
                <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/1st photo.jpg" class="img-fluid">
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 p-4">
                <h4>How do you create a Cinnamon Maker profile that stands out?</h4>
                <ul class="no-bullets">
                    <li> 
                        <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/1st ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Take your time building your profile to ensure that it is exactly as you desire.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/2nd ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Connect to your relevant professional organizations to boost your credibility.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/3rd ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Deliver an accurate description of the experience you will provide to assist you get more customers.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/4th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Show me what you look like! Put up a profile picture that shows your face clearly.
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/5th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - We may ask you to show your ID so that everyone can feel safe in our community.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
    </div>
    <div class="section-2 row">
        <div class="col-lg-8 p-4">
            <h4>Who we are in Cinnamon?</h4>
            <h6>Cinnamon Makers are enthusiastic people who may give individual, families, especially those with children, a memorable and exciting opportunity to try something new. Here are the traits of a Cinnamon Maker:</h6>
            <ul class="no-bullets">
                <li>
                    C - Creative – Able to deliver unique and creative experiences
                </li>
                <li>
                    I -  Intuitive – Able to discern or understand the situation or customer at the onset
                </li>
                <li>
                    N - Nurturing – Takes good care of the customer and has the customer’s welfare in mind
                </li>
                <li>
                    N - Neighborly – Is a good “neighbor” by creating a safe space for the customer
                </li>
                <li>
                    A - Adaptable – Can come up with alternative ideas when the need arises; Can adjust based on the situation
                </li>
                <li>
                    M - Munificent – Generous in sharing knowledge and experience so that the customer would really see the experience as worth its cost
                </li>
                <li>
                    O - Open – Has a listening ear to his/her customers. Able to receive feedback well, whether positive or negative
                </li>
                <li>
                    N - Notable – Can create a notable or memorable experience for the customers
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 pt-5">
                <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/2nd photo.jpg" class="img-fluid">
            </div>
    </div>
    <div class="section-3 row">
        <div class="col-lg-4 pt-5">
            <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/3rd photo.jpg" class="img-fluid">
        </div>
        <div class="col-lg-8 p-4">
            <h4>Now, let's talk about what you should stay away from</h4>
            <ul class="no-bullets">
                <li>
                    <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/6th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> -  Giving any false or misleading information about who you are.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/7th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Asking to pay the fees outside of the Cinnamon platform.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/8th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Creating more than one account. Always remember that you can make more experiences.
                </li>
                <li>
                    <img src="images/Cinnamon Maker/9th ICON.png" class="img-icon text-center"> - Offering a service that is outside the set boundaries of Cinnamon.
                </li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
<Footer></Footer>
